**Rate of Return**

\[
\text{Rate of Return} = \frac{\text{Revenue} - \text{Cost}}{\text{Cost}}
\]

\[
= \frac{15{,}000 - 22{,}000}{22{,}000}
= \frac{-7{,}000}{22{,}000}
\approx -0.318 \; (\text{or } -31.8\%)
\]

So the business is operating at a **–31.8 % rate of return** (a loss relative to its cost).
